# Reference — TA: Kingdoms Weapons

Every `[WEAPONn]` sub-section harvested from every `units/*.fbi`.
TA:K embeds weapon stats directly inside each unit's FBI rather than
maintaining a separate `weapons/` directory like TA does, so each row
here is tied to exactly one owner unit.

**{{.TotalWeapons}} weapon definitions** across **{{.UnitsWithWeapon}}
weapon-bearing units**.

Each weapon's `Owner` is the `unitname=` of the FBI it lives in.
`Slot` is the `[WEAPONn]` section name within that FBI (units carry up
to three slots). `Type` is the inline `type=` field, typically
`Ballistic`, `Missile`, `Magical`, or `Melee`. `Range` is in pixels;
`Damage` is the `[DAMAGE].default` value (per-target overrides exist
but are not shown).

Column definitions are documented in the kbot format docs:

- **TDF format** (the on-disk syntax these fields live in) — see
  [FBI / TDF / OTA](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/tdf.md)
  in the kbot documentation.
- **Weapon archetype taxonomy** — see
  [Gamedata: weapons.tdf reference](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/gamedata.md#weaponstdf--weapon-tdf-reference).
- **How weapons hook into units** — the inline `[WEAPONn]` model is
  TA:K-specific; TA uses a separate `weapons/*.tdf` directory instead
  (see the
  [TA vs TA:K matrix](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/compare.md)).

Cross-reference unit codes with [TA:K unit IDs](tak-units.md).

